{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792494585,"nonce":"1VW2EGKtA2nj8k/0kdH+7gamDcI=","message":"Implemented Explorer panels and local recovery.\n\nThe file browser is the top resizable pane without an extra collapsible header. Outline, Timeline and Dependencies use native Ashui Collapsible and vertical Resizable components. Their heights and open state survive sidebar rebuilds; collapsed contents and background jobs are released. Tree rows use the Explorer's compact 12-pixel level offset and 24-pixel row height. Timeline stays flat. Headers align left; tools remain icon buttons with tooltips.\n\nOutline uses Haxe compiler module symbols, including unsaved input, with debounced cancelable jobs. Clicks navigate through the editor's existing goTo action. Remix box-2, t-box, code-block, instance and node-tree icons distinguish classes, types, methods, fields/variables and namespaces, with theme-aware colors.\n\nDependencies resolves libraries declared in the build using background haxelib jobs from the workspace directory; source folders load on expansion and source files open in editor tabs. Refresh and Libraries settings are header tools.\n\nTimeline is a native composition of local history and the Git extension's explorer view contribution. The new view.visibility hook is replayed on subscribe and reported on attach/detach. The Git cursor follows file renames on HEAD's first-parent history, searches in bounded pages and closes on hide. Late loads cannot replace the current file's cursor.\n\nLocal patch journals under .rayde/history preserve never-staged edits, abandoned states after Undo, and the bounded data-only CodeHistory undo/redo stacks. Writes are atomic and throttled to 350 ms, with close/shutdown flushes. Recovery checks the saved disk baseline; external changes remain in place and become the new baseline. Journal paths follow Explorer renames. Revision tabs are read-only and mount only while active; restoring is an undoable edit to the unsaved buffer. Retention is 200 changes plus baseline, with an 8 MiB per-file checkpoint cap. The persistence adapter targets the pinned Ashui history format without retaining editor instances or owners.\n\nValidation:\n- scripts/check.sh passed, including compiler Outline nesting, local restart recovery, external-change baselines, abandoned edit states, renamed journals, bounded compaction and malformed checkpoints.\n- scripts/check-git.sh passed, including file-history paging, rename following, unborn HEAD, missing paths and closed cursors, plus the existing Git backend suite.\n- Explorer, basic file-browser, document lifecycle, Git and Theme Studio snapshot scenarios passed in both schemes.\n- Explorer click tests verify the method declaration caret position and a library source opening in a tab; resizing, collapse height restoration, hide/reopen cleanup, local revision preview, undoable restore and persisted redo also pass. Captures show zero compositing layers and no pointer hooks.\n- Native executable and macOS app preview rebuilt using existing shared native dependency builds; no worktrees or extra Cargo target directories.\n\nPreview images: bin/explorer-panels/rayde-{dark,light}-explorer-panels.png and rayde-{dark,light}-explorer-library-source.png.\n\nLanded on main in commit 99d38d4beda9263851668167c6c8e5667c4c7fe6.","files":null}]}